1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,521
You're drifting off to sleep… then JOLT!

2
00:00:02,521 --> 00:00:04,111
Your whole body jerks awake.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:07,838
It has a name: a hypnic jerk, or sleep start.

4
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:09,794
Most people get them now and then.

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:15,474
As you fall asleep, your muscles relax and your brain shifts into sleep mode.

6
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:21,827
Scientists think the brain may misread that relaxing as falling, and fires a sudden jolt.

7
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:27,081
They're more likely with caffeine, stress, being overtired, or a late workout.

8
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,189
They're harmless.

9
00:00:29,189 --> 00:00:32,559
Less caffeine late in the day and a regular bedtime can help.

10
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:39,873
See a doctor if jerks keep you from sleeping, happen during the day, or come with tongue biting or confusion.
